Upstream licence and provenance — lib/set_kb/

The retrieval core in this package is a PORT (a derivation by translation, not
a verbatim copy) of MIT-licensed upstream code: an upstream `kb` package, taken
via an intermediate TypeScript port that itself carried the notice below. A
Python translation of that logic is a derivative work, so the licence notice
travels even though no line of the original source text survives here.

Per decision of 2026-10-07 recorded in openspec/changes/kb-search/design.md,
set-core's public tree credits the upstream with the MIT copyright line only —
it does not name the upstream repository or organisation beyond that line. The
upstream commit SHA is kept because it is the reference that identifies the
exact source tree the port was taken from, without naming anything.

