## Port lineage

upstream (TypeScript, `packages/kb/src/`)
  → an intermediate TypeScript port (fork; divergences listed below)
  → this package (Python, standard library only, `sqlite3` + FTS5)

Divergences carried from the intermediate TypeScript port: the query tokenizer
accepts every Unicode letter/number (an ASCII-only tokenizer wipes out accented
queries), the language-pack seam with shipped Hungarian stopwords, the lane
semantics (a named-channel reserved lane), the excluded-tree defaults (agent
logs out, the archive in), the chunk parent link resolved after merge/split,
and the upstream trust/DOX machinery deliberately dropped.

Divergences added by this port: NFC path normalisation, a sorted (reproducible)
walk order, and — from the change's design (D8) — an EMPTY `laneChannels`
means NO reserved lane, where the intermediate port fell back to a lane for
agent-instruction files.

## Per-file attribution

Every ported module carries a one-line reference to this file in its header,
as the first line. Modules that are new (written for set-core, not carried
over) do NOT carry that line — the distinction is what makes the attribution
meaningful.

